  "final_answer": "I have gathered comprehensive information. Based on my research on ArXiv, the cs.NE (Neural and Evolutionary Computing) new submissions page shows the listings for Friday, 25 September 2026.\n\n## Answer\n\nThe **latest research paper about neural networks** submitted within the last week on ArXiv is:\n\n**arXiv:2609.30115** — *\"Orbital Error Dynamics: Self-Organized Criticality, Ephemeral Parameter Resonance, and Non-Linear Biological Ontologies in Zero-Storage Neural Synthesis\"*\n\n- **Authors:** Volkan Dağlı, Zerrin Dağlı, Dağhan Dağlı\n- **Submitted:** 24 September 2026 (within the last week relative to ArXiv's current date of 25 September 2026)\n- **Subjects:** Neural and Evolutionary Computing (cs.NE); Machine Learning (cs.LG); Chaotic Dynamics (nlin.CD)\n- **Comments:** Official National Patent Priority: TR 2026/016285 (Filed Sept 22, 2026). Foundational companion theory to Mandelbrot Fractal Neural Synthesis.\n\n### Why this paper\nThe paper is clearly about neural networks (its abstract opens: *\"Modern deep neural networks treat parameters as static floating-point matrices stored in physical memory...\"*). It is the **newest entry** in the cs.NE category — the dedicated ArXiv category for \"Neural and Evolutionary Computing\" research — and it has the highest arXiv ID (2609.30115) among the four new cs.NE submissions on 25 September 2026:\n\n| # | arXiv ID | Title |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 2609.29016 | EvoTreeNAD: Genealogy-Guided Evolution for LLM-Driven Neural Architecture Discovery |\n| 2 | 2609.29755 | On Growth and Form, and Function: Reusable Regulatory Handles Control Phenotypic Variation |\n| 3 | 2609.30102 | Activation-Flexible ANN-to-SNN Conversion with Finite-State Markov Neurons |\n| 4 | **2609.30115** | **Orbital Error Dynamics: … Zero-Storage Neural Synthesis** ← latest |\n\nThe paper proposes a new analytical framework (Orbital Error Dynamics) for synthesizing neural networks without storing weight matrices, validated on the Two-Moons manifold dataset.",
